-- Discovery diagnostic codes.
--
-- A diagnostic row stores its code and a block of integer arguments; the
-- message is rendered from both at the boundary that shows it, so the text
-- lives in one place.
---
What a discovery diagnostic reports, and the meaning of its arguments:

- `UnresolvedImportDiagnostic`: An import names a module no source provider has. Arguments: the `ImportId` of the import.
- `SourceTooLargeDiagnostic`: A source is too large for its spans to be packed. Arguments: the source's byte length.
- `TooManySourcesDiagnostic`: Discovery reached more sources than a span can number. No arguments.
- `UnterminatedDocstringDiagnostic`: A `---` docstring has no closing `---` line. No arguments.
- `UnterminatedStringDiagnostic`: A string literal reaches the end of the source. No arguments.
- `MultilineStringDiagnostic`: A string literal reaches the end of its line. No arguments.
- `UnknownEscapeDiagnostic`: A backslash escape names no escape. Arguments: the escaped byte.
- `UnterminatedEscapeDiagnostic`: A backslash is the last byte of the source. No arguments.
- `UnicodeEscapeDigitCountDiagnostic`: A `\u{...}` escape has no digits or more than six. No arguments.
- `UnicodeEscapeNonHexDiagnostic`: A `\u{...}` escape holds a non-hex character. No arguments.
- `UnterminatedUnicodeEscapeDiagnostic`: A `\u{...}` escape reaches the end of the source. No arguments.
- `UnicodeCodepointOutOfRangeDiagnostic`: A `\u{...}` escape names a surrogate or a value above U+10FFFF. No arguments.
- `MultilineRawStringDiagnostic`: A raw string literal reaches the end of its line. No arguments.
- `UnterminatedRawStringDiagnostic`: A raw string literal reaches the end of the source. No arguments.
- `InterpolationTooDeepDiagnostic`: Interpolation holes nest more deeply than the lexer allows. Arguments: the depth limit.
- `InterpolatedEscapeAtEndDiagnostic`: An interpolated string ends in a backslash at the end of the source. No arguments.
- `MultilineInterpolatedStringDiagnostic`: An interpolated string reaches the end of its line. No arguments.
- `UnterminatedInterpolatedStringDiagnostic`: An interpolated string reaches the end of the source. No arguments.
- `InvalidCharLiteralDiagnostic`: A character literal does not hold exactly one character. No arguments.
- `UnterminatedCharLiteralDiagnostic`: A character literal reaches the end of the source. No arguments.
- `IntegerLiteralOverflowDiagnostic`: An integer literal exceeds the Int128 range. Arguments: the `LiteralId` of its digits.
- `UnexpectedByteDiagnostic`: A byte starts no token and no UTF-8 character. Arguments: the byte.
- `UnexpectedCharacterDiagnostic`: A character starts no token; the span covers it. No arguments.
- `InconsistentIndentationDiagnostic`: A dedent returns to no enclosing indentation level. No arguments.
- `UnresolvedRootDiagnostic`: A root request names a module no source provider has. No arguments; the row is a root diagnostic.
- `ImportCaseMismatchDiagnostic`: An import names a module that exists only under different letter case. Arguments: the `ImportId` of the import, then the `PathId` of the path below the resolving directory as the source provider stores it (the text to write instead).
- `RootCaseMismatchDiagnostic`: A root request names a source that exists only under different letter case. Arguments: the `PathId` of the file name as the source provider stores it; the row is a root diagnostic.
- `UnverifiableSpellingDiagnostic`: A source exists but a directory on the way to it could not be listed, so its spelling could not be checked. Arguments: the `ImportId` of the requesting import; none for a root.
- `UnreadableSourceDiagnostic`: A source the provider located could not be read. Arguments: the `ImportId` of the requesting import; none for a root.
- `ExpectedColonAfterImportDiagnostic`: `import` is not followed by `:`. No arguments.
- `ExpectedNewlineAfterImportHeaderDiagnostic`: `import:` is not followed by a new line. No arguments.
- `ExpectedIndentedImportsDiagnostic`: The import items are not indented under `import:`. No arguments.
- `ExpectedModulePathDiagnostic`: An import item does not start with a module path, or a `/` is not followed by a path part. No arguments.
- `ExpectedImportSymbolDiagnostic`: A selected symbol is not a name. No arguments.
- `ExpectedCommaBetweenImportSymbolsDiagnostic`: Two selected symbols are not separated by `,`. No arguments.
- `ExpectedConstructorNameDiagnostic`: A `name(...)` selection lists no constructor, or lists a non-name. No arguments.
- `ExpectedClosingParenAfterConstructorsDiagnostic`: A `name(...)` selection is not closed by `)`. No arguments.
- `ExpectedAliasNameDiagnostic`: `as` is not followed by a name, or is followed by a reserved keyword. No arguments.
- `ExpectedImportSymbolsAfterColonDiagnostic`: The `:` after a module path is followed by neither symbols nor an indented symbol block. No arguments.
- `ReservedKeywordAsNameDiagnostic`: A reserved keyword is written where a name belongs; the span covers it and parsing continues as if it were the name. No arguments.
- `ExpectedNameDiagnostic`: A name is required here (a declaration, member, parameter, type parameter, trait, bound or supertrait name) and none is written. No arguments.
- `ExpectedDimensionDiagnostic`: A dimension (`#N`, `#3`, `#_` or a dimension expression) is required and none is written. No arguments.
- `ExpectedTypeDiagnostic`: A type is required and none is written. No arguments.
- `ArrayDimensionsExpectedDiagnostic`: An array suffix `[...]` holds something other than dimensions. No arguments.
- `TupleArityDiagnostic`: A tuple type or tuple binder has fewer than two or more than four elements. No arguments.
- `UnionVariantTooManyFieldsDiagnostic`: A union variant declares more payload fields than a variant's ownership bitmask has bits for; the span is the variant's name. No arguments.
- `ExpectedColonDiagnostic`: `:` is required here. No arguments.
- `ExpectedCommaDiagnostic`: `,` is required between two items. No arguments.
- `ExpectedLeftParenDiagnostic`: `(` is required here. No arguments.
- `ExpectedRightParenDiagnostic`: `)` is required here. No arguments.
- `ExpectedRightBracketDiagnostic`: `]` is required here. No arguments.
- `ExpectedLeftBraceDiagnostic`: `{` is required here. No arguments.
- `ExpectedRightBraceDiagnostic`: `}` is required here. No arguments.
- `ExpectedArrowDiagnostic`: `->` is required here. No arguments.
- `ExpectedEqualDiagnostic`: `=` is required here. No arguments.
- `ExpectedEqualEqualDiagnostic`: `==` is required in a dimension constraint. No arguments.
- `ExpectedHashDiagnostic`: `#` is required before a dimension. No arguments.
- `ExpectedNewlineDiagnostic`: A new line is required here. No arguments.
- `ExpectedIndentDiagnostic`: An indented block is required here. No arguments.
- `ExpectedKeywordDiagnostic`: A keyword (`func`, `type`, `alias`, `for`, `builtin`, `in` after a loop variable, or `from` after a select receive binding) is required here; the span shows where. No arguments.
- `UnknownAnnotationDiagnostic`: An `@annotation` names no annotation the language defines. No arguments.
- `AnnotationArgumentsDiagnostic`: A function annotation is written with arguments. No arguments.
- `AnnotationWithoutFunctionDiagnostic`: Annotations are not followed by a function declaration. No arguments.
- `ExpectedDeclarationDiagnostic`: A top-level item does not start a declaration. No arguments.
- `ForeignFunctionOutsideBlockDiagnostic`: `foreign func` is written without a `foreign:` block. No arguments.
- `ExpectedForeignArgumentDiagnostic`: A foreign block's parentheses hold no argument. No arguments.
- `ExpectedForeignArgumentValueDiagnostic`: A foreign block argument's value is not a string literal. No arguments.
- `ExpectedForeignFunctionDiagnostic`: A foreign block holds something other than a function signature. No arguments.
- `ExpectedForeignCNameDiagnostic`: `=` after a foreign function signature is not followed by a string literal. No arguments.
- `ExpectedCleanupBuiltinNameDiagnostic`: A resource type's `builtin(...)` does not hold a string literal. No arguments.
- `BuiltinTypeArgumentsDiagnostic`: A non-resource builtin type declaration is written with arguments. No arguments.
- `ExpectedSupertraitOrMethodsDiagnostic`: `trait Name:` is followed by neither supertraits nor a method block. No arguments.
- `ExpectedImplMethodDiagnostic`: An `implements` block holds something other than a method. No arguments.
- `ExpectedExpressionDiagnostic`: An expression is required here and none is written. No arguments.
- `ExpectedPatternDiagnostic`: A match pattern is required here and none is written. No arguments.
- `ExpectedNumberAfterMinusDiagnostic`: `-` in a pattern is not followed by a number literal. No arguments.
- `ExpectedSpreadTargetDiagnostic`: `...` in a list pattern is followed by neither a name nor `_`. No arguments.
- `ExpectedAssignmentOperatorDiagnostic`: A typed name in statement position is followed by no `=`, `?=` or compound assignment. No arguments.
- `DiscardedQuestionBindDiagnostic`: `_ ?= value` binds the unwrapped value to `_`. No arguments.
- `FieldAssignmentDiagnostic`: `x.field = value` assigns to a field; record update syntax is required. No arguments.
- `ExpectedBuiltinNameDiagnostic`: `builtin(` is not followed by a string literal name. No arguments.
- `RemovedIntoConversionDiagnostic`: `into Type(...)` is the removed spelling of `into_opaque Type(...)`. No arguments.
- `RemovedFromConversionDiagnostic`: `from Type(...)` is the removed spelling of `from_opaque Type(...)`. No arguments.
- `RemovedTypeAscriptionDiagnostic`: `value as Type` is removed; the span covers `as`, and parsing skips the type. No arguments.
- `ExpectedConcurrentParameterDiagnostic`: The parentheses after `concurrent` or `concurrently` hold no parameter. No arguments.
- `ConcurrentForTupleBinderDiagnostic`: `for (a, b) in xs concurrently` has more than one loop variable. No arguments.
- `ConcurrentDuplicateParameterDiagnostic`: A concurrency parameter name appears twice in one parameter list. No arguments.
- `ConcurrentUnknownParameterDiagnostic`: `concurrent(...)` holds a name other than `max_threads` or `timeout`. No arguments.
- `ConcurrentForUnknownParameterDiagnostic`: `concurrently(...)` holds a name other than `limit` or `timeout`. No arguments.
- `ConcurrentForMaxThreadsDiagnostic`: `concurrently(...)` holds `max_threads`, which belongs to `concurrent(...)`. No arguments.
- `ConcurrentMaxThreadsNotPositiveLiteralDiagnostic`: `max_threads` is not a positive integer literal. No arguments.
- `ConcurrentLimitNotPositiveLiteralDiagnostic`: `limit` is not a positive integer literal. No arguments.
- `ConcurrentForMissingLimitDiagnostic`: A non-empty `concurrently(...)` list has no `limit`. No arguments.
- `WithMultipleBindingsDiagnostic`: A `with` header binds more than one resource. No arguments.
- `ExpectedFatArrowDiagnostic`: `=>` is required here. No arguments.
- `InterpolationHoleNotExpressionDiagnostic`: An interpolation hole holds more than one expression. No arguments.
- `InterpolatedStringPatternDiagnostic`: A string with `${...}` holes is written as a match pattern. No arguments.
- `QuestionBindInLoopDiagnostic`: `name ?= value` is written inside a `while`, `for` or `for ... concurrently` body; the span is the `?=`. No arguments.
- `BreakOutsideLoopDiagnostic`: `break` is written outside every loop body, or in a function body nested in one; the span is the keyword. No arguments.
- `ContinueOutsideLoopDiagnostic`: `continue` is written outside every loop body, or in a function body nested in one; the span is the keyword. No arguments.
---
enum DiscoveryDiagnosticCode:
	UnresolvedImportDiagnostic
	SourceTooLargeDiagnostic
	TooManySourcesDiagnostic
	UnterminatedDocstringDiagnostic
	UnterminatedStringDiagnostic
	MultilineStringDiagnostic
	UnknownEscapeDiagnostic
	UnterminatedEscapeDiagnostic
	UnicodeEscapeDigitCountDiagnostic
	UnicodeEscapeNonHexDiagnostic
	UnterminatedUnicodeEscapeDiagnostic
	UnicodeCodepointOutOfRangeDiagnostic
	MultilineRawStringDiagnostic
	UnterminatedRawStringDiagnostic
	InterpolationTooDeepDiagnostic
	InterpolatedEscapeAtEndDiagnostic
	MultilineInterpolatedStringDiagnostic
	UnterminatedInterpolatedStringDiagnostic
	InvalidCharLiteralDiagnostic
	UnterminatedCharLiteralDiagnostic
	IntegerLiteralOverflowDiagnostic
	UnexpectedByteDiagnostic
	UnexpectedCharacterDiagnostic
	InconsistentIndentationDiagnostic
	UnresolvedRootDiagnostic
	ImportCaseMismatchDiagnostic
	RootCaseMismatchDiagnostic
	UnverifiableSpellingDiagnostic
	UnreadableSourceDiagnostic
	ExpectedColonAfterImportDiagnostic
	ExpectedNewlineAfterImportHeaderDiagnostic
	ExpectedIndentedImportsDiagnostic
	ExpectedModulePathDiagnostic
	ExpectedImportSymbolDiagnostic
	ExpectedCommaBetweenImportSymbolsDiagnostic
	ExpectedConstructorNameDiagnostic
	ExpectedClosingParenAfterConstructorsDiagnostic
	ExpectedAliasNameDiagnostic
	ExpectedImportSymbolsAfterColonDiagnostic
	ReservedKeywordAsNameDiagnostic
	ExpectedNameDiagnostic
	ExpectedDimensionDiagnostic
	ExpectedTypeDiagnostic
	ArrayDimensionsExpectedDiagnostic
	TupleArityDiagnostic
	UnionVariantTooManyFieldsDiagnostic
	ExpectedColonDiagnostic
	ExpectedCommaDiagnostic
	ExpectedLeftParenDiagnostic
	ExpectedRightParenDiagnostic
	ExpectedRightBracketDiagnostic
	ExpectedLeftBraceDiagnostic
	ExpectedRightBraceDiagnostic
	ExpectedArrowDiagnostic
	ExpectedEqualDiagnostic
	ExpectedEqualEqualDiagnostic
	ExpectedHashDiagnostic
	ExpectedNewlineDiagnostic
	ExpectedIndentDiagnostic
	ExpectedKeywordDiagnostic
	UnknownAnnotationDiagnostic
	AnnotationArgumentsDiagnostic
	AnnotationWithoutFunctionDiagnostic
	ExpectedDeclarationDiagnostic
	ForeignFunctionOutsideBlockDiagnostic
	ExpectedForeignArgumentDiagnostic
	ExpectedForeignArgumentValueDiagnostic
	ExpectedForeignFunctionDiagnostic
	ExpectedForeignCNameDiagnostic
	ExpectedCleanupBuiltinNameDiagnostic
	BuiltinTypeArgumentsDiagnostic
	ExpectedSupertraitOrMethodsDiagnostic
	ExpectedImplMethodDiagnostic
	ExpectedExpressionDiagnostic
	ExpectedPatternDiagnostic
	ExpectedNumberAfterMinusDiagnostic
	ExpectedSpreadTargetDiagnostic
	ExpectedAssignmentOperatorDiagnostic
	DiscardedQuestionBindDiagnostic
	FieldAssignmentDiagnostic
	ExpectedBuiltinNameDiagnostic
	RemovedIntoConversionDiagnostic
	RemovedFromConversionDiagnostic
	RemovedTypeAscriptionDiagnostic
	ExpectedConcurrentParameterDiagnostic
	ConcurrentForTupleBinderDiagnostic
	ConcurrentDuplicateParameterDiagnostic
	ConcurrentUnknownParameterDiagnostic
	ConcurrentForUnknownParameterDiagnostic
	ConcurrentForMaxThreadsDiagnostic
	ConcurrentMaxThreadsNotPositiveLiteralDiagnostic
	ConcurrentLimitNotPositiveLiteralDiagnostic
	ConcurrentForMissingLimitDiagnostic
	WithMultipleBindingsDiagnostic
	ExpectedFatArrowDiagnostic
	InterpolationHoleNotExpressionDiagnostic
	InterpolatedStringPatternDiagnostic
	QuestionBindInLoopDiagnostic
	BreakOutsideLoopDiagnostic
	ContinueOutsideLoopDiagnostic


---
A stable name for each code, for dumps and fixtures.
---
pure func diagnostic_code_name(code: DiscoveryDiagnosticCode) -> String:
	match code:
		UnresolvedImportDiagnostic:
			"UnresolvedImportDiagnostic"
		SourceTooLargeDiagnostic:
			"SourceTooLargeDiagnostic"
		TooManySourcesDiagnostic:
			"TooManySourcesDiagnostic"
		UnterminatedDocstringDiagnostic:
